  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 102 AM EDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nWet pattern will continue through at least the middle of next week. \nThe upper level low will linger in the eastern Gulf and then \neventually lift up into the broader upper level flow early next \nweek. Meanwhile, South FL will remain under a ribbon of enhanced \nmoisture. High PoPs (70-90%) are expected each day, with the highest \nchances being during the afternoon and early evening hours each day. \nUrban flooding will continue to be a concern each day, especially as \nsoils remain moist and additional rainfall is added onto them each \nday. \n\nWith the expected rainfall and cloud cover, temperatures during the \nextended period will be near normal with highs generally in the \nupper 80s to lower 90s, and low temps ranging from the lower 70s \nover the interior to upper 70s along the coasts.",
